    <bpmn:process id="W_W1168" name="W1168. Direct Store Delivery (DSD) Receiving, Verification &amp; Vendor Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: DSD vendor truck arrives at store receiving dock with purchase order delivery
Frequency: ~500–600 DSD receipts/month across all stores (~2–3 DSD deliveries per store per month)
Volume: ~3 DSD deliveries/store/month × 200 stores = ~600 receipts/month; higher volume at stores near cement plants and lumber mills
Owner: Receiving Clerk / Stock Associate
Participants: Stock Associate (receiving), Department Supervisor, AP Clerk (3-way match), Category Manager (vendor compliance)
Source: workflow W1168 — Direct Store Delivery (DSD) Receiving, Verification &amp; Vendor Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1168_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1168_Lane1" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1168_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1168_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1168_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1168_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1168_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1168_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1168_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1168_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1168_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1168_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1168_Start4" name="DSD vendor truck arrives at store receiving dock with purchase order delivery">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1168_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1168_Task5" name="Pre-delivery coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-delivery coordination: System sends DSD delivery schedule to store 24 hours in advance based on vendor ASN; Stock Associate reviews expected deliveries for the day; confirms dock/receiving area availability; coordinates with Department Supervisor for heavy/bulky items requiring forklift or additional labor
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1168_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1168_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1168_Task6" name="Vendor arrival &amp; check-in">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor arrival &amp; check-in: DSD vendor truck arrives at store receiving dock; Stock Associate verifies: (a) delivery against scheduled DSD PO — vendor name, PO number, expected items; (b) driver identity and vehicle condition; (c) for cement/lumber/sand: verify truck weight ticket matches PO quantity; (d) direct vendor to designated unloading area
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1168_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1168_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1168_Task7" name="Unloading &amp; quantity verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Unloading &amp; quantity verification: (a) Stock Associate supervises unloading; counts pieces/units as they come off the truck; (b) for bulk items (sand, gravel): verify volume against weight ticket conversion; (c) for lumber: verify board feet per piece against PO specification; (d) for cement: count bags and check for torn/wet bags; (e) for appliances: verify model numbers and serial numbers against PO; (f) flag any quantity discrepancy (&gt; 2% tolerance) immediately
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Vendor Driver
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1168_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1168_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1168_Task8" name="Quality inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quality inspection: Stock Associate inspects DSD goods: (a) cement bags: check for moisture damage, clumping, or expired manufacturing date (cement has 3-month shelf life from production); (b) lumber: check for warping, cracks, and grade stamps; (c) structural steel: verify dimensions and grade markings; (d) reject non-conforming items — document with photos and note on delivery receipt
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1168_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1168_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1168_Task9" name="Goods receipt processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Goods receipt processing: Stock Associate processes goods receipt on handheld tablet: (a) scan PO barcode or enter PO number; (b) enter actual received quantities per line; (c) note any discrepancies (short shipment, over-shipment, quality rejects); (d) capture electronic signature from vendor driver acknowledging receipt; (e) system updates store inventory and creates AP voucher for 3-way match per W244
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1168_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1168_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1168_Task10" name="Putaway to sales floor">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Putaway to sales floor: Stock Associate moves DSD goods directly to sales floor or designated outdoor storage area (lumber yard, cement staging); no backroom storage for DSD items — sell-from-shelf model; update bin location in system
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 20–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1168_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1168_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1168_Task11" name="DSD vendor compliance tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: DSD vendor compliance tracking: System captures DSD delivery performance data: (a) on-time delivery % (delivered within scheduled window), (b) quantity accuracy % (shipped vs. ordered), (c) quality rejection rate, (d) documentation completeness; feeds vendor scorecard per W44 and SCP-020; Category Manager reviews DSD vendor compliance monthly
Responsible (R): System / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 15 min/month/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1168_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1168_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1168_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1168_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1168_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-256 (ensure controlled execution — Outbound Distribution (PA-06.1).) | - operational: Receiving Clerk / Stock Associate review and approval gate
Owner: Receiving Clerk / Stock Associate</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1168_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1168_Annotation13" targetRef="W1168_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1168_Flow15" sourceRef="W1168_Start4" targetRef="W1168_Task5" />
