    <bpmn:process id="W_W1169" name="W1169. Import Container Inbound Logistics, Port Drayage &amp; DC Delivery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Import container cleared by customs per W464 and released from port/terminal for delivery to DC
Frequency: ~400–600 TEUs/month; ~20–30 containers per DC per week
Volume: ~15–25 container drayage moves per DC per week; peak during pre-Ber months (July–August) and pre-summer (February–March) build-ups
Owner: Inbound Logistics Coordinator
Participants: Inbound Logistics Coordinator, Customs Broker, Drayage Carrier, DC Receiving Supervisor, Import Coordinator, Finance (duty payment)
Source: workflow W1169 — Import Container Inbound Logistics, Port Drayage &amp; DC Delivery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1169_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1169_Lane1" name="Customs Broker">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1169_Lane2" name="Inbound Logistics Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1169_Lane3" name="Drayage Carrier Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1169_Lane4" name="Drayage Carrier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1169_Lane5" name="DC Receiving Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1169_Lane6" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1169_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1169_Start8" name="Import container cleared by customs per W464 and released from port/terminal for delivery…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1169_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1169_Task9" name="Container release tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Container release tracking: Customs Broker confirms container release from Bureau of Customs per W464; Inbound Logistics Coordinator receives release notification; verifies: (a) container number, (b) bill of lading, (c) free time expiry date (demurrage risk per W249), (d) destination DC; enters container into &quot;Drayage Queue&quot; in ERP with priority based on free time remaining
Responsible (R): Customs Broker / Inbound Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Import Coordinator
Duration: 30 min/container</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1169_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1169_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1169_Task10" name="Drayage carrier booking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Drayage carrier booking: Inbound Logistics Coordinator books drayage carrier: (a) select from approved drayage carriers based on port location, chassis availability, and DC destination; (b) confirm truck availability within 24 hours of release for containers with &lt; 3 days free time remaining; (c) provide container details, port pickup location, and DC delivery address; (d) for overweight containers (tiles, cement, steel): ensure carrier has appropriate truck capacity (10-wheeler with 20ft container chassis or 40ft chassis for FCL)
Responsible (R): Inbound Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 30 min/container</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1169_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1169_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1169_Task11" name="Port pickup &amp; inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Port pickup &amp; inspection: Drayage carrier picks up container from port terminal; driver conducts visual inspection: (a) verify container seal number matches bill of lading; (b) check for visible damage (dents, holes, water intrusion); (c) photograph container condition and seal at port gate; (d) flag discrepancies immediately to Inbound Logistics Coordinator
Responsible (R): Drayage Carrier Driver
Accountable (A): Inbound Logistics Coordinator
Duration: 2–4 hours (port processing)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1169_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1169_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1169_Task12" name="Inland transit &amp; truck ban management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Inland transit &amp; truck ban management: Carrier transports container from port to DC; system tracks via telematics per W199; route planning accounts for: (a) LGU truck ban restrictions per W431; (b) port-to-DC route typically 2–4 hours for Metro Manila ports to Laguna/Clark DCs; (c) Cebu port to Mandaue DC: 1 hour; (d) Davao Sasa Wharf to Davao DC: 30 min; (e) system provides live ETA to DC Receiving Supervisor
Responsible (R): Drayage Carrier / System
Accountable (A): DC Dispatch
Duration: 1–4 hours transit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1169_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1169_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1169_Task13" name="DC receiving appointment &amp; unloading">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: DC receiving appointment &amp; unloading: Container arrives at DC; DC Receiving Supervisor verifies: (a) container seal number, (b) external condition; schedules unloading per W585 dock appointment; DC team unloads container: (a) full container load: 2–4 hours for manual unloading of 20ft container; (b) verify item counts and SKUs against import PO and packing list per W3; (c) flag any damage or shortage discovered during unloading; (d) process goods receipt in WMS
Responsible (R): DC Receiving Supervisor / DC Team
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/container</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1169_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1169_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1169_Task14" name="Empty container return">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Empty container return: After unloading, drayage carrier must return empty container to port/depot within carrier&#x27;s free time (typically 48–72 hours); Inbound Logistics Coordinator tracks empty return to avoid per diem charges; confirm return with carrier; close drayage order in system
Responsible (R): Drayage Carrier / Inbound Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1169_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1169_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1169_Task15" name="Demurrage &amp; detention monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Demurrage &amp; detention monitoring: System tracks container free time countdown: (a) port demurrage: free time starts at vessel discharge; standard rate PHP 5,000–8,000/day after free time; (b) carrier detention: free time starts at container gate-out; standard rate PHP 2,000–4,000/day; (c) weekly report of containers at risk of demurrage; escalate at-risk containers to VP Supply Chain for expedited drayage; (d) demurrage costs tracked per W249 and reported monthly
Responsible (R): System / Inbound Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1169_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1169_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1169_Task16" name="Monthly drayage analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly drayage analytics: Inbound Logistics Coordinator compiles drayage performance: (a) average port-to-DC cycle time by port, (b) demurrage incidence and cost, (c) carrier on-time pickup rate, (d) container damage rate, (e) cost per TEU by lane; benchmark against prior period
Responsible (R): Inbound Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1169_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1169_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1169_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1169_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1169_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-256 (ensure controlled execution — Outbound Distribution (PA-06.1).) | - operational: Inbound Logistics Coordinator review and approval gate
Owner: Inbound Logistics Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1169_Assoc19" sourceRef="W1169_Annotation18" targetRef="W1169_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
