    <bpmn:process id="W_W1315" name="W1315. Delivery Vehicle Loading Optimization, Weight Compliance &amp; LTFRB Regulation Adherence" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Outbound delivery truck loading at DC; or LTFRB (Land Transportation Franchising and Regulatory Board) roadside inspection; or vehicle weight monitoring alert
Frequency: Daily loading optimization at each DC (4 DCs); ongoing weight compliance per trip; LTFRB inspections are random but frequent on Philippine highways
Volume: ~50–80 outbound delivery trips per DC per day; ~200–320 trips/day chain-wide; vehicle types: 10-wheeler wing vans (max 18T payload), 6-wheeler trucks (max 8T payload)
Owner: DC Dispatch Coordinator
Participants: DC Dispatch Coordinator, Truck Driver, Loading Team Lead, Transportation Planner, Third-Party Fleet Manager
Source: workflow W1315 — Delivery Vehicle Loading Optimization, Weight Compliance &amp; LTFRB Regulation Adherence</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1315_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1315_Lane1" name="Transportation Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1315_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1315_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1315_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1315_Lane2" name="Loading Team Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1315_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1315_Lane3" name="DC Dispatch Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1315_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1315_Lane4" name="Truck Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1315_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1315_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1315_Start6" name="Outbound delivery truck loading at DC; or LTFRB (Land Transportation Franchising and…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1315_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1315_Task7" name="Route-based load planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Route-based load planning: (a) Transportation Planner creates daily delivery routes per DC: (i) group store replenishment orders into delivery routes (2–3 stores per route for 10-wheeler; 1–2 stores for 6-wheeler) per W15, (ii) sequence stops for optimal driving distance, (iii) consider special handling: heavy items (cement, tiles) on bottom, fragile items on top, hazardous materials (paint, chemicals) separated per W492; (b) DC Dispatch Coordinator plans load for each route: (i) system calculates total order weight per route: sum of all item weights across all stops, (ii) system compares to vehicle payload capacity: flag if &gt; 90% of max payload (margin for weight estimation error), (iii) if overloaded: split route (move one store&#x27;s delivery to another truck) or upgrade vehicle (6-wheeler → 10-wheeler), (iv) system generates load plan: item × quantity × stop sequence × bay position
Responsible (R): Transportation Planner / DC Dispatch Coordinator
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 30–60 min/route</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1315_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1315_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1315_Task8" name="Loading execution &amp; weight verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Loading execution &amp; weight verification: (a) Loading Team Lead loads truck per load plan: (i) load in reverse-stop sequence (last delivery stop loaded first, deepest in the truck), (ii) heavy items loaded first (bottom/front), light items last (top/rear), (iii) secure cargo: strap and block to prevent shifting during transit (critical for Philippine roads with potholes, rough surfaces, and steep inclines in mountainous areas like Bukidnon, Benguet); (b) after loading: (i) drive truck to DC weighbridge (scale) — record actual gross vehicle weight, (ii) compare to legal GVW limit: if GVW exceeds limit by &gt; 500 kg: remove items from load and schedule for next trip; (iii) if within limit: record weight on dispatch manifest, (iii) system records actual weight vs. planned weight for load planning accuracy tracking
Responsible (R): Loading Team Lead / Truck Driver
Accountable (A): DC Dispatch Coordinator
Duration: Per truck: 30–60 min loading + 10 min weighbridge</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1315_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1315_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1315_Task9" name="LTFRB compliance documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: LTFRB compliance documentation: (a) each truck carries required documentation: (i) delivery manifest with store names, items, and quantities, (ii) cargo manifest (for LTFRB inspection: proof that goods are for BuildRight&#x27;s own use and not for-hire cargo — BuildRight trucks carry own inventory, not third-party freight), (iii) vehicle registration and LTFRB franchise (for owned trucks) or certificate of public convenience (for third-party trucks), (iv) driver&#x27;s license and medical certificate, (v) insurance certificate; (b) for third-party trucks: Third-Party Fleet Manager ensures compliance: (i) valid LTFRB franchise for the vehicle class, (ii) vehicle roadworthiness (annual LTFRB inspection), (iii) driver qualification (professional driver&#x27;s license with restriction code 8 for heavy vehicles); (c) DC Dispatch Coordinator verifies documentation completeness before truck dispatch
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch Coordinator / Third-Party Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 5–10 min/truck</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1315_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1315_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1315_Task10" name="Roadside weight compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Roadside weight compliance: (a) during transit, truck may encounter: (i) LTFRB/DPWH roadside weigh station (common on national highways: NLEX, SLEX, STAR Tollway, CAVITEX), (ii) LGU checkpoint with portable weigh scales (common on provincial roads entering municipalities), (iii) private toll road weight enforcement (e.g., NLEX Corporation enforces strict weight limits); (b) if flagged for overweight: (i) driver presents manifest and cargo documentation, (ii) if overloaded: driver pays fine on-site (PHP 5,000–15,000), (iii) truck may be required to offload excess cargo at the weigh station — driver calls DC Dispatch Coordinator for pickup arrangement, (iv) incident logged in fleet management system for root cause analysis (load planning error, route change adding weight, unauthorized additional pickup)
Responsible (R): Truck Driver / DC Dispatch Coordinator
Accountable (A): Transportation Planner
Duration: Per incident: 1–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1315_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1315_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1315_Task11" name="Loading optimization analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Loading optimization analytics: (a) monthly: Transportation Planner analyzes loading metrics: (i) average payload utilization (% of max payload actually used — target: 80–90%), (ii) overweight incidents: frequency, cause, fine cost, (iii) load planning accuracy: actual weight vs. planned weight variance, (iv) vehicle type utilization: are 6-wheelers being used efficiently or should more routes use 10-wheelers?, (v) multi-stop efficiency: average number of stops per route and impact on loading sequence accuracy; (b) recommendations: (i) adjust vehicle assignment for consistently overloaded routes, (ii) split high-weight store deliveries across multiple trips, (iii) negotiate higher-payload vehicles with third-party fleet providers, (iv) optimize product mix per trip (balance heavy and light items)
Responsible (R): Transportation Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1315_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1315_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1315_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1315_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1315_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-178 (ensure fleet compliance &amp; freight-cost integrity.) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: DC Dispatch Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1315_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1315_Annotation13" targetRef="W1315_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1315_Flow15" sourceRef="W1315_Start6" targetRef="W1315_Task7" />
