    <bpmn:process id="W_W1514" name="W1514. Inter-Island Emergency Cargo Air Freight &amp; Charter Coordination for Critical Stock Replenishment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Typhoon or earthquake disrupts regular inter-island RoRo/ferry routes for 3+ days, (b) DC-to-store stockout of critical construction materials with no alternate DC source, (c) VIP project customer deadline requiring emergency material delivery to island store
Frequency: ~8–12 emergency air freight activations/year (seasonal: 60% during typhoon season Jun–Nov)
Volume: 1–5 tons per activation; PHP 200K–1.5M per shipment air freight cost
Owner: Logistics Manager
Participants: Logistics Manager, Transportation Planner, DC Operations Manager, Category Manager, Finance Controller, 3PL Air Freight Broker
Source: workflow W1514 — Inter-Island Emergency Cargo Air Freight &amp; Charter Coordination for Critical Stock Replenishment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1514_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1514_Lane1" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1514_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1514_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1514_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1514_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1514_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1514_Lane2" name="Transportation Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1514_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1514_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1514_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1514_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1514_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1514_Start5" name="(a) Typhoon or earthquake disrupts regular inter-island RoRo/ferry routes for 3+ days…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1514_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1514_Task6" name="Emergency trigger assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Emergency trigger assessment: (a) Logistics Manager receives alert: either typhoon disruption notice from PAGASA/shipping lines, store stockout report from Store Manager, or VIP project escalation from Sales Rep; (b) assess: (i) which stores affected, (ii) which critical SKUs at risk (cement, GI sheets, electrical wire, lumber — typically ~50–100 SKUs classified as &quot;air-freight eligible&quot;), (iii) estimated duration of sea freight disruption, (iv) revenue impact of stockout (PHP/day lost per store per SKU)
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1514_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1514_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1514_Task7" name="Cost-benefit authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cost-benefit authorization: (a) Transportation Planner calculates: air freight cost (PHP/kg × estimated weight) vs. estimated lost revenue from stockout (days of disruption × daily sales per SKU × store count); (b) Logistics Manager presents authorization request to VP Supply Chain: (i) total shipment cost, (ii) revenue protected, (iii) ROI breakeven point; (c) VP Supply Chain approves if: air freight cost &lt; projected lost revenue, OR customer is VIP project account with &gt; PHP 500K contract value at risk
Responsible (R): Transportation Planner / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1514_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1514_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1514_Task8" name="Shipment coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Shipment coordination: (a) Logistics Manager contacts 3PL air freight broker for cargo space on next available flight (Philippine Airlines Cargo, Cebu Pacific Cargo, or charter if &gt; 3 tons); (b) confirms: flight schedule, cargo cutoff time, weight/volume limits, hazmat restrictions (cement and paint may have air cargo restrictions); (c) DC Operations Manager arranges emergency pick-pack: prioritize air-freight-eligible SKUs, pack on pallets suitable for air cargo ULD loading
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / DC Ops Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1514_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1514_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1514_Task9" name="Documentation &amp; compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Documentation &amp; compliance: (a) Transportation Planner prepares: airway bill, packing list, CAAP hazmat declaration if applicable, store delivery manifest; (b) for charter flights: coordinate CAAP charter permit, landing rights at destination airport; (c) Finance Controller validates payment terms with air freight broker and approves petty cash / fund transfer for destination-side trucking (airport to store)
Responsible (R): Transportation Planner / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1514_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1514_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1514_Task10" name="Shipment execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Shipment execution: (a) DC dispatches cargo to origin airport; (b) air freight broker confirms loading and departure; (c) Logistics Manager notifies destination Store Manager of arrival time and pickup instructions; (d) Store Manager arranges truck pickup from airport to store (typically 10-wheeler or 6-wheeler hire from local transport provider)
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Transit: 2–8 hours flight + 2–4 hours ground</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1514_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1514_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1514_Task11" name="Receiving &amp; reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Receiving &amp; reconciliation: (a) Store receives cargo; verifies against airway bill packing list; (b) system receives goods into store inventory with &quot;Emergency Air Freight&quot; receipt type for cost tracking; (c) Logistics Manager confirms delivery completion; (d) Finance Controller records air freight cost against store logistics cost center for monthly review
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1514_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1514_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1514_Task12" name="Post-event review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-event review (monthly): Logistics Manager reviews all emergency air freight activations: (a) total cost vs. revenue protected, (b) average response time (trigger to delivery), (c) recurring routes or SKUs that could justify pre-positioning buffer stock to reduce future air freight dependency
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1–2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1514_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1514_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1514_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1514_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1514_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-256 (ensure controlled execution — Outbound Distribution (PA-06.1).) | - operational: Logistics Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Logistics Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1514_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1514_Annotation14" targetRef="W1514_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1514_Flow16" sourceRef="W1514_Start5" targetRef="W1514_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1514_Flow17" sourceRef="W1514_Task6" targetRef="W1514_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1514_Flow18" sourceRef="W1514_Task7" targetRef="W1514_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1514_Flow19" sourceRef="W1514_Task8" targetRef="W1514_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1514_Flow20" sourceRef="W1514_Task9" targetRef="W1514_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1514_Flow21" sourceRef="W1514_Task10" targetRef="W1514_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1514_Flow22" sourceRef="W1514_Task11" targetRef="W1514_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1514_Flow23" sourceRef="W1514_Task12" targetRef="W1514_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1514_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1514_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1514">
